  "_about": "The ingredient model for 'what can I cook?' (docs/HOME-ENGINE.md §8). parents: a specific ingredient points at its generic one, so the specific always covers the generic (cheddar covers 'tasty cheese' asked for as grated cheese; spaghetti covers 'pasta'). varieties: generics that also cover all their children, because a cook who has 'potatoes' or 'pasta' can use any kind. substitutes: groups that stand in for each other with partial credit only, counted as covered only when the cook turns substitutes on. aliases: extra AU/UK/US names for typing a pantry list. relinks: fixes for the recipe generator's bad links (whole fish linked to 'whole', salt cod to 'salt'); 'unknown:' means a real thing the database doesn't have, which always counts as missing. oils: staples that count as always in only while the cook's 'oil' switch is on.",
